    "note": "Enrolled version (HB 2005-C); House 35-24 on 2023-05-02, Senate 17-3 on 2023-06-15, repassed House 34-14 on 2023-06-21. The under-21 possession ban and the public-building change that appear in earlier versions are not in the enrolled text (age stays 18 in ORS 166.250 (1)(c)(A)). Section 8 amends section 4 so that unserialized possession is covered by the same penalty ladder, operative September 1, 2024 (section 10); section 9 does the same for section 5. Section 11 appropriates $356,816 to State Police to implement the Act; emergency clause in section 12. Section 7 also amends the dealer-transfer process of ORS 166.412 for permit holders."
